 Now I understand the data structure:\n\nFor farmers_markets:\n- state_name, state_abbr, farmers_markets (int64), and other columns\n- I need to sum the farmers_markets column excluding territories\n\nFor census_population:\n- NAME (state/region name), POPESTIMATE2025 (2025 population)\n- I need to find the row where NAME = \"United States\"\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Get the total farmers markets (excluding territories) from the farmers_markets alias\n2. Get the 2025 US population from the census_population alias\n3. Compute the ratio: (total_farmers_markets / us_population) * 100,000\n4. Verify both values and the computed metric\n\nLet me first get a peek at the data to understand what \"territories\" are in the first dataset.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01UbXsGUBTYChx5EXFpTdzyd","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_abbr', 'state_name', 'farmers_markets').limit(20)"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":319,"cacheRead":15423,"cacheWrite":1462,"totalTokens":17218,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.001595,"cacheRead":0.0015423000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.0018275,"total":0.0049788},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":195},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912000037,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74DSgSYjvmwzn9E8hc6","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01UbXsGUBTYChx5EXFpTdzyd","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_abbr\",\"state_name\",\"farmers_markets\"\n\"CA\",\"California\",647\n\"NY\",\"New York\",555\n\"PA\",\"Pennsylvania\",426\n\"MN\",\"Minnesota\",390\n\"IL\",\"Illinois\",370\n\"VA\",\"Virginia\",336\n\"WI\",\"Wisconsin\",335\n\"MI\",\"Michigan\",321\n\"MA\",\"Massachusetts\",273\n\"FL\",\"Florida\",246\n\"GA\",\"Georgia\",231\n\"OH\",\"Ohio\",219\n\"TX\",\"Texas\",216\n\"MO\",\"Missouri\",208\n\"NC\",\"North Carolina\",196\n\"IA\",\"Iowa\",194\n\"KY\",\"Kentucky\",183\n\"IN\",\"Indiana\",181\n\"CO\",\"Colorado\",164\n\"WA\",\"Washington\",159\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912005714},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I see states. Let me check if there are territories by looking for rows that might be territories like \"District of Columbia\", \"Puerto Rico\", \"Virgin Islands\", etc.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Ndiky7TvumvzRBL8yES41g","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.select('state_abbr', 'state_name', 'farmers_markets')","limit":0}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":180,"cacheRead":16885,"cacheWrite":501,"totalTokens":17579,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0009000000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0016885000000000001,"cacheWrite":0.00062625,"total":0.00322775},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":42},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912005714,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74Dqwg8zyeFJ3bLtBYN","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Ndiky7TvumvzRBL8yES41g","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"state_abbr\",\"state_name\",\"farmers_markets\"\n\"CA\",\"California\",647\n\"NY\",\"New York\",555\n\"PA\",\"Pennsylvania\",426\n\"MN\",\"Minnesota\",390\n\"IL\",\"Illinois\",370\n\"VA\",\"Virginia\",336\n\"WI\",\"Wisconsin\",335\n\"MI\",\"Michigan\",321\n\"MA\",\"Massachusetts\",273\n\"FL\",\"Florida\",246\n\"GA\",\"Georgia\",231\n\"OH\",\"Ohio\",219\n\"TX\",\"Texas\",216\n\"MO\",\"Missouri\",208\n\"NC\",\"North Carolina\",196\n\"IA\",\"Iowa\",194\n\"KY\",\"Kentucky\",183\n\"IN\",\"Indiana\",181\n\"CO\",\"Colorado\",164\n\"WA\",\"Washington\",159\n\"MD\",\"Maryland\",140\n\"CT\",\"Connecticut\",124\n\"KS\",\"Kansas\",123\n\"OR\",\"Oregon\",122\n\"AL\",\"Alabama\",115\n\"OK\",\"Oklahoma\",102\n\"AZ\",\"Arizona\",97\n\"TN\",\"Tennessee\",95\n\"SC\",\"South Carolina\",86\n\"NJ\",\"New Jersey\",84\n\"MT\",\"Montana\",78\n\"AR\",\"Arkansas\",77\n\"LA\",\"Louisiana\",73\n\"VT\",\"Vermont\",71\n\"AK\",\"Alaska\",59\n\"ID\",\"Idaho\",59\n\"WV\",\"West Virginia\",57\n\"WY\",\"Wyoming\",57\n\"NE\",\"Nebraska\",55\n\"DC\",\"District Of Columbia\",54\n\"NH\",\"New Hampshire\",50\n\"MS\",\"Mississippi\",49\n\"DE\",\"Delaware\",49\n\"ME\",\"Maine\",43\n\"NM\",\"New Mexico\",34\n\"RI\",\"Rhode Island\",33\n\"UT\",\"Utah\",30\n\"NV\",\"Nevada\",28\n\"ND\",\"North Dakota\",18\n\"SD\",\"South Dakota\",17\n\"HI\",\"Hawaii\",13\n\"PR\",\"Puerto Rico\",2\n\"VI\",\"Virgin Islands\",0\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912009018},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I can see the data includes:\n- US states (50)\n- DC (District of Columbia) - which may or may not be considered a territory\n- PR (Puerto Rico) - which is a territory\n- VI (Virgin Islands) - which is a territory\n\nThe user asked for \"excl. territories\", so I need to exclude PR and VI. The question is whether to include DC. Typically, DC is included when people refer to \"the U.S.\" (50 states + DC), but territories refer to Puerto Rico, Virgin Islands, Guam, etc. However, the user specifically said to exclude territories, so I should interpret this as excluding PR and VI. Let me check if there are any other territories.\n\nLooking at the state abbreviations, I see:\n- PR = Puerto Rico (territory)\n- VI = Virgin Islands (territory)\n\nThese are clearly the territories mentioned. The 50 states plus DC should be included. So I should sum the farmers_markets column where state_abbr is NOT in ['PR', 'VI'].\n\nNow let me get the total farmers markets excluding territories.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01CyCxY8zD8pKiuHiNVSUQ9t","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter((source.state_abbr != 'PR') & (source.state_abbr != 'VI')).aggregate(total_farmers_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":13,"output":390,"cacheRead":17386,"cacheWrite":619,"totalTokens":18408,"cost":{"input":0.000013,"output":0.0019500000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0017386,"cacheWrite":0.00077375,"total":0.00447535},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":245},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912009018,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74E69CXNh7UguLTaCXp","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01CyCxY8zD8pKiuHiNVSUQ9t","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"xorq_select: select: ValueError: disallowed expression: BitAnd (the safe evaluator rejects `&`/`|` — chain filters instead: source.filter(a).filter(b))\n"}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1786912013935},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to chain the filters instead of using & operator. Let me fix that.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01HjrWMNX5kjNGbAvT7xwkwR","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"farmers_markets","compose":"source.filter(source.state_abbr != 'PR').filter(source.state_abbr != 'VI').aggregate(total_farmers_markets=source.farmers_markets.sum())"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":166,"cacheRead":18005,"cacheWrite":464,"totalTokens":18649,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.0008300000000000001,"cacheRead":0.0018005000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.00058,"total":0.0032245},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":22},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912013936,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74ETyMu7xdrkiTtDFdP","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01HjrWMNX5kjNGbAvT7xwkwR","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"total_farmers_markets\"\n7942\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912017561},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! The total number of farmers markets excluding territories (PR and VI) is 7,942.\n\nNow I need to get the 2025 US population from the census_population alias. I need to find the row where NAME = \"United States\" and get POPESTIMATE2025.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_0131BGH5MZHp67WtaooLE8hT","name":"xorq_select","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog","on":"census_population","compose":"source.filter(source.NAME == 'United States').select('NAME', 'POPESTIMATE2025')"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":194,"cacheRead":18469,"cacheWrite":216,"totalTokens":18891,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.00097,"cacheRead":0.0018469,"cacheWrite":0.00027,"total":0.0030989},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":68},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912017562,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74EkHPFJemY3XW9FxXx","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_0131BGH5MZHp67WtaooLE8hT","toolName":"xorq_select","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"NAME\",\"POPESTIMATE2025\"\n\"United States\",341784857\n\n(showing up to 50 rows; pass limit or aggregate to count — do not page)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786912021770},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! The 2025 US population is 341,784,857.\n\nNow I need to create a build script that computes the metric: farmers markets per 100,000 residents. This is a cross-dataset metric, so I need to follow the pattern from the xorq-catalog skill.\n\nThe formula is: (7942 / 341784857) * 100000\n\nLet me create a build script that reads both sources, joins them (with a constant key since we're doing a whole-table total vs a single reference row), and computes the metric.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BuEU2Q2P9cwaaUiu31JF1T","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_farmers_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener()\n_o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]\nu.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\n\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\nfact = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"farmers_markets\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\nref = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con,\n    table_name=\"census_population\",\n    storage_options=so,\n)\n\n# Aggregate farmers markets excluding territories (PR, VI)\nfact_total = (\n    fact.filter(fact.state_abbr != 'PR')\n    .filter(fact.state_abbr != 'VI')\n    .aggregate(total_farmers_markets=fact.farmers_markets.sum())\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Get US population for 2025\nref_us = (\n    ref.filter(ref.NAME == 'United States')\n    .select('POPESTIMATE2025')\n    .mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n)\n\n# Join and calculate rate per 100,000\nexpr = (\n    fact_total.join(ref_us, fact_total.k == ref_us.k)\n    .mutate(farmers_markets_per_100k=fact_total.total_farmers_markets / ref_us.POPESTIMATE2025 * 100000)\n    .select('total_farmers_markets', 'POPESTIMATE2025', 'farmers_markets_per_100k')\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":740,"cacheRead":18685,"cacheWrite":250,"totalTokens":19687,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.0037,"cacheRead":0.0018685000000000002,"cacheWrite":0.0003125,"total":0.005893000000000001},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":130},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786912021771,"responseId":"msg_011Ce74F3iNzYaBy7KX7ihXe","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BuEU2Q2P9cwaaUiu31JF1T","toolName":"write","content":